   "title": "My God, the Creator!",
   "summary": "The name “Elohim” describes God as the Creator. In other words, our God is the creator of the world and everything that exist in it.",
   "key_scripture": "Genesis 1:1",
   "key_scripture_text": "In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "The name “Elohim” describes God as the Creator. In other words, our God is the creator of the world and everything that exist in it. Many scientists have propounded theories to explain how the world came into being and even the existence of human beings. In spite of theories like the “Big Bang” and the “Evolution”, it is an undisputable fact that God created the world. Atheists may claim that there is no God but the fact still holds that there is a God in Heaven that rules over the affairs of men (Psalm 8:3, Psalm 102:25, Col. 1;16-17). Daniel 4:17 says, “This matter is by the decree of the watchers, and the demand by the word of the holy ones: to the intent that the living may know that the Most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will, and setteth up over it the basest of men.”"
