     "text": "Ωbirth of Isaac. I want you to put yourself in the position of Abraham. Imagine the joy and excitement that Abraham experienced as he watched his son grow. Then one day God demanded for the only son of old man Abraham ((Gen. 22:2). Many modern-day people would have disobeyed this command but without hesitation, Abraham took Isaac and they embarked on a three-day journey to Mount Mariah. It was certainly a journey of no return for Isaac. As they walked along Isaac said, “Father I see the fire and the wood, but where is the lamb for the sacrifice? Abraham was so confident in his God that he knew the he could provide even at the last moment and in the most difficult of times. True to his faith, God provided a ram on top of a mountain."
    },
