   "title": "Be Determined to Please God!",
   "summary": "In the journey of life, your only one desire must be to please God in all you do. Rather than struggling to impress people, strive to do what is right. One of the dangers of life is to try to confuse the applause of men with the affirmation of Heaven.",
   "key_scripture": "Galatians 1:10",
   "key_scripture_text": "For do I now persuade men, or God? Or do I seek to please men? For if I still pleased men, I would not be a bondservant of Christ.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "In the journey of life, your only one desire must be to please God in all you do. Rather than struggling to impress people, strive to do what is right. One of the dangers of life is to try to confuse the applause of men with the affirmation of Heaven. However, what you must know is that, men may applaud you but may be God might have rejected you. What is popular with men may be unpopular with God. Daniel and his friends purposed in their hearts not to defile themselves...Daniel 1:8"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Therefore, simply keep doing what is right and you will come out of the pressure of pleasing people. Those who do right things don’t ever fear been faulted by men because doing it right has already earned them God’s approval. Right doing is what gives you your right place in the school of life. Keep doing what is right and you will never fear any evil."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "You must choose to rather obey God than to please men. This is what the Jewish elders wanted the disciples to do. However, Peter the leader of the disciples and the others responded in Ac 5:29 this way, ‘...We ought to obey God rather than men.’ In this wicked and perverse generations where sin is on the ascendancy and morality has been jettisoned somewhere there must be a new breed of people who will always be determined to please God rather than men."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "You must never follow the multitude to do evil (Exodus 23:2) because the majority is not always right. In fact, they are mostly wrong. Decide to stand up for God! Never blend with the world because whoever is a friend of the world is an automatic enemy of God (James 4:4)"
    }
