   "title": "The Saving Grace",
   "summary": "Grace simply means undeserved or unmerited favour. It simply means when God does for you what you don’t deserve.",
   "key_scripture": "Titus 3:7",
   "key_scripture_text": "That being justified by his grace, we should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Grace simply means undeserved or unmerited favour. It simply means when God does for you what you don’t deserve. Jesus Christ is the custodian of Grace and therefore when you get connected to Him, you are expected to flow in unending and exceeding Grace - John 1:17, ‘For the law was given by Moses, but grace and truth came by Jesus Christ.’ There is the Saving dimension of Grace. The greatest gift that Heaven gave humanity is salvation and it was by an act of Grace. How can you explain this; that a chronic sinner has simply become a celebrated saint. We were all living in sin until we experienced an extension of the hands of Grace upon our lives - Titus 3:7, ‘That being justified by his grace, we should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.’"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Titus 2:11-14 also says ‘11 ¶ For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men, 12 Teaching us that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly, righteously, and godly, in this present world; 13 Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great God and our Saviour Jesus Christ; 14 Who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a peculiar people, zealous of good works.’"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "As a Christian, you must always pray for the saving Grace to flow to the masses who don’t know Jesus and you must help others to experience the saving Grace by sharing the Gospel with them."
    }
   ],
