   "summary": "Those who dominate in the spiritual realm will automatically dominate in the physical realm. This is because everything is a spiritual situation before it becomes a physical condition. In this New Year, you must be fervent in spirit.",
   "key_scripture": "Romans 12:11",
   "key_scripture_text": "Not slothful in business; fervent in spirit; serving the Lord;",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Those who dominate in the spiritual realm will automatically dominate in the physical realm. This is because everything is a spiritual situation before it becomes a physical condition. In this New Year, you must be fervent in spirit. This simply means, you must not joke with your spiritual life. Never allow the activities and the busy-ness of life to kill your relationship and intimacy with God. To be fervent in spirit, you must engage in the following spiritual exercises"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "1. Be Persistent in Prayer: To be persistent means to hold firm or"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "steadfastly to something. Despite the odds, obstacles, defeats and set-backs, you stick to it. A classic example in the Bible is blind Bartimaeus. He screamed, ‘Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me’ People in the crowd said, ‘Shut up and die in your blindness’. He ignored them and simply kept on crying to Jesus until he was called out of the crowd. This year, ignore all the anti-prayer agents in your life (TV, too much conversation, too much sleep, etc) and continue to scream to God in prayer if you want to make it."
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "text": "Study the Bible : Joshua 1:8 says ‘This Book of the Law shall"
    },
