    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Joseph had many justifiable reasons to hold a grudge against his brothers; he loved them enough to send them food but they hated him enough to sell him as a slave to foreigners. He however decided to forget all their acts of wickedness against him. Joseph named his first son Manasseh meaning, I have forgotten and named his second son Ephraim which means fruitfulness – Gen. 41:51-52."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "By this act, Joseph revealed the secret to being fruitful in the land of suffering – Forgetting the past. Unless you forget the past, you can never enter into the glorious future God has designed for you. You must be determined never to become a prisoner of your past; whether past failures or victories. You can simply not be driving on the highway of life and be looking back; you will have a fatal accident if you do that."
