     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Most people fail in life not because they lack knowledge or talent but because they quit . When problems seem insurmountable, quitting may look like the easiest way out. It is true for every marriage, ministry, job and relationship. The lack of persistence is the trait of losers. Life is a race and in the race of life we run with endurance. Even Jesus Christ had to endure the pains of the cross in order that He might obtain the joy that was set before Him (Hebrews 12:1-2)."
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "The Apostle Paul was a man who run with endurance. In spite of all the challenges He faced in life, he still did not give up. In II Corinthians 4:8-9, he wrote, ‘8 ¶ We are hard pressed on every side, yet not crushed; we are perplexed, but not in despair; 9 persecuted, but not forsaken; struck down, but not destroyed’"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "At the end of the journey of his life; the Apostle Paul emerged victorious in spite of all the odds he faced - In II Timothy 4:7-8, he said triumphantly ‘ I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith.8 Finally, there is laid up for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will give to me on that Day, and not to me only but also to all who have loved His appearing.’"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "One man said, ‘A man is a hero not because he is braver than anyone else, but because he is brave for ten minutes longer’."
